-- title:
--   Original BV uniform physical generator and raw-jump residual sum is nonpositive
-- statement:
--   For the literal original bounded-variation Lévy process, original ruin-stopped uniform grid and any integrable or nonintegrable residual B given by the exact generator-plus-raw-negative-jump formula, the residual is almost surely nonpositive for every grid level. The generator cells are nonpositive by the source HJB inequality, and the raw jump-removal correction is nonpositive because the genuine BV physical remainder is almost surely monotone and its predictable derivative/discount weights are nonnegative.
-- source:
--   Independent source-exact sign bridge using Proved monotone original raw remainder e9d95081 and Proved HJB generator grid sign 52591942, for the actual residual in 965af42c.

